4. The system shall declare a winner if a player successfully places three matching symbols in a row.
5. The system shall detect and declare a draw if the grid is filled and no player has formed a line.
6. The system shall provide feedback at the end of the game, indicating whether the first player (X) or the second player (O) won, or if the game ended in a draw.
7. The system shall allow players to restart the game after a match is over to play again.
8. The system shall include a timer that tracks the duration of the match.
